GLOBAL LAYOUT NOTES FOR LANDING PAGE IMPLEMENTATION

Page background: #FBF6EE throughout — no white, no gray.
Max content width: Approximately 1100–1200px centered, with generous horizontal padding on mobile.
Section spacing: Generous vertical padding between sections (80–120px desktop, 48–64px mobile).
Images: All photography should maintain warm amber/terracotta color grading. Avoid cool-toned or desaturated images.
Badges/Labels: Small uppercase pill badges above section headings. Solid fill using #B57152 or #50352B with white or light text.
Dividers: Thin horizontal rules (#D7C2AA or #B39A7D) used sparingly to separate sub-sections within a card.
Tables: Bordered style with #B57152 header text. Keep clean and minimal.
Diagrams/Smart Layouts: Recreate as custom HTML/CSS components or SVG. The rings diagram (Section 3) should be a circular icon-grid. The numbered boxes (Section 4) should use circular number badges at the top of each card.
Mobile responsiveness: All multi-column layouts (Sections 1, 2, 3, 4) should stack vertically on mobile. Images should appear above text on mobile.
No harsh shadows or gradients — keep the aesthetic flat, warm, and editorial.
Font recommendation: A warm serif or humanist sans-serif typeface pairs best with this palette. Consider Playfair Display (headings) + Lato or Inter (body) as a starting point.
Tone: Premium, calm, intelligent. Not aggressive SaaS. Not corporate. Think: a trusted advisor presenting a proposal over coffee.
- FIGMA STRUCTURE REQUIREMENT: Every section, row, and multi-element card MUST be built using Figma Auto Layout. Set explicit vertical and horizontal resizing constraints (e.g., Hug contents or Fill container).
- BUTTON COMPONENTS: All Call-to-Action (CTA) elements must be built as a component with 16px vertical and 32px horizontal padding, rounded corners (4px radius), filled with #B57152, and text colored #FBF6EE.
- COMPONENT SPACING: Set universal Auto Layout gaps: 24px between items inside cards, 48px between grid elements, and 96px margins between major sections.

IMPORTANT
- MODIFICATION & EDITING REQUIREMENT: Do not flatten, rasterize, or lock any layers, groups, or components. Everything must remain 100% open and editable.
- NO VECTOR BLOCKS: Tables, grids, and the Concentric Rings diagram must be constructed entirely out of individual, editable Auto Layout frames, text layers, and stroke vectors. Do not generate them as single SVG icons or flattened shapes.
- TEXT INTEGRITY: All textual content must be rendered as raw, native Figma text layers. Do not convert text into outlines or vector paths.
- FRAME GROUPING: Use Auto Layout Frames instead of traditional Groups (Cmd+G) to organize sections, ensuring that paddings, margins, and content blocks can be adjusted manually post-generation.
